# The receiver's DPI/profile buttons are reported via the keyboard HID usage
# page on interface 1, so udev's input_id tags that interface ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD=1.
# UPower's sibling-discovery type guesser (up-device-supply.c) ranks Keyboard
# above Mouse unconditionally once any sibling reports it, so the genuine
# ID_INPUT_MOUSE=1 on interface 0 never wins. Strip the false keyboard tag so
# UPower is left with only the correct mouse signal.
#
# DRIVERS=="keychron" alone is enough to scope this to our own bound
# interfaces (interface 0's real mouse input has no ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD tag to
# begin with, so this is a no-op there) — bInterfaceNumber can't be combined
# with DRIVERS here since they live on different parent devices, and udev
# only matches parent-device keys against a single common ancestor.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", DRIVERS=="keychron", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}="0"
